-- EXPECT-ERROR: cannot be widened
-- R4a — SIBLINGS: neither subsumes the other (2026-08-06).
--
-- `IO.FileRead` and `IO.FileWrite` are siblings under `IO.FileSystem`.
-- Neither is an ancestor of the other, so this is not attenuation in either
-- direction — it is a lateral move, and a lateral move is authority the holder
-- was never given.
--
-- Separate from reject/t153 because the two fail different halves of the
-- check. t153's source (`IO.Console`) is strictly NARROWER than its target;
-- here the two are simply unrelated. A check written as "reject when the
-- target subsumes the source" catches t153 and lets this through; only
-- "require the SOURCE to subsume the target" catches both.
mod Siblings do
  needs IO

  pfn sideways(r : Cap(IO.FileRead)) : Cap(IO.FileWrite) do
    cap_narrow(r)
  end

  fn main(cap : Cap(IO)) do
    println("file-read cannot become file-write")
  end
end
